🏛️ How to Explain the Dual-Platform Architecture (Snowflake + Databricks)
When asked: "Why did you use both Snowflake and Databricks, and how do they fit together?"
🗣️ Spoken Voice Track:
"We chose a purpose-built dual platform architecture based on workload strengths:
Snowflake (Enterprise BIW Data Warehouse):
Role: Central source of truth for business intelligence, financial reporting, and executive analytics.
Strengths: Exceptional SQL performance for structured Kimball Star Schemas, zero-management compute scaling, strict RBAC governance, and seamless view presentation for BI tools like PowerBI.

Databricks (Product Feature Store & ML Platform):
Role: Distributed feature computation engine and feature repository for machine learning models.
Strengths: Distributed PySpark processing for complex feature transformations, native integration with MLflow / Unity Catalog Feature Store, and Delta Lake time-travel capabilities essential for Point-in-Time feature joins.

The Bridge (Bi-directional Sync & Shared Delta Lake):
Upstream source systems (RMS, MRL) land in raw Delta storage in Azure.
Databricks runs heavy feature engineering pipelines (window functions, rolling aggregations, lagging price elasticities) and registers them in the Databricks Feature Store.
Curated feature aggregates and conformed dimension outputs are synchronized into Snowflake BIW_DWH via Snowflake Spark Connectors / Delta Sharing, allowing BI analysts to query feature metrics directly alongside financial reports."*


